<x-layout title="Community and publishing terms"><div class="legal-page"><h1>Publishing and community terms</h1><div class="prose"><p>These are the publishing principles for this Folkscript installation. The operator must finalize their legal identity, jurisdiction, membership pricing, billing terms, and contact details before a public launch.</p><h2>Your writing belongs to you</h2><p>Publish only material you have the right to share. By publishing, you allow this installation to display and distribute your story, its metadata, and previews through its reading experience, feeds, and discovery features.</p><h2>Participate thoughtfully</h2><p>Be honest about your identity and sources. Do not post harassment, threats, private information without consent, unlawful material, or content that infringes another person’s rights. Add to a conversation rather than disrupting it.</p><h2>Moderation and access</h2><p>Editors may review reports, hide comments, archive stories, or restrict accounts. You can report a concern from an article’s conversation section. Publishing requires a verified account and the appropriate author permissions.</p><h2>Membership</h2><p>Membership is available only when the operator enables billing. The checkout page provides the final price and recurring payment terms. Members can manage an active subscription through the billing portal. Creator payouts depend on a configured payment provider and onboarding.</p><h2>Keep an original copy</h2><p>You are responsible for maintaining a copy of your writing. Revision history is a convenience within the platform and does not replace your own backup.</p></div></div></x-layout>
